  "releaseNotes": "10.0.84\n- Builds for .NET 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10.\n- Fixed: the consumer dispatcher slept 200 ms or more before every next batch of deliveries (ConsumerWorkService), throughput with prefetchCount 5 grew from ~25 to ~15 000 msg/s.\n- Handler workers (degreeOfParallelism > 1) wake up on a signal instead of polling the queue with sleeps up to 1 s.\n- Send/Publish overloads with persistent: false send transient messages (delivery mode 1) that the broker does not write to disk.\n- RabbitMQ port: \"port\" in the rabbitMQ section or the connection string, and \"host:port\" per host; 5672 by default.\n- Handler setting internalQueueFormat: \"journal\" stores the local queue in append-only segment files instead of a file per message; \"files\" stays the default, old .q files are read in both modes.",
